quiet.md #3: load KaTeX symbol fonts without an "m" glyph

KaTeX's symbol faces (Size1-4, AMS, Caligraphic, Script) have no lowercase
letters and were refused by the "has an m" check, so formulas fell back to
other fonts.

diff --git a/crates/gpui_apple/src/text_system.rs b/crates/gpui_apple/src/text_system.rs
index 63dd0fc62fb3dd21c87826842e9eb2c137c9f01f..9eee3e5e1a22de4a7496d106415e35fb1d802013 100644
--- a/crates/gpui_apple/src/text_system.rs
+++ b/crates/gpui_apple/src/text_system.rs
@@ -311,8 +311,11 @@ impl AppleTextSystemState {
                 // but we need to be able to load it for rendering Windows icons in
                 // the Storybook (on macOS).
                 let is_segoe_fluent_icons = font.full_name() == "Segoe Fluent Icons";
+                // quiet.md: KaTeX's symbol faces (Size1-4, AMS, Caligraphic,
+                // Script) have no lowercase letters.
+                let is_katex = font.full_name().starts_with("KaTeX_");
 
-                if !has_m_glyph && !is_segoe_fluent_icons {
+                if !has_m_glyph && !is_segoe_fluent_icons && !is_katex {
                     // I spent far too long trying to track down why a font missing the 'm'
                     // character wasn't loading. This log statement will hopefully save
